    "id": "007-93_01",
    "stac_version": "1.1.0",
    "description": "The dataset contains twelve samples (of about five days each) of tropospheric\naerosol less than < 3 micrometer fractionated into five particle diameter\nranges (Dp: 2.84, 2.04, 1.4, 0.8, 0.441 micrometer) and a backup filter\ncollecting all particles < 0.41 micrometer, and samples of all precipitation\nduring the sampled period. They were taken at King George Island, Antarctica,\nfrom January 29 to March 27, 1995, during the XXXII Chilean Scientific\nAntarctic Expedition. The sampler was located near the sea at the top of a 60-m\nhigh hill. Chemical analysis of the samples includes quantification of the\nspecies present in the soluble and insoluble fractions. In the last case, an\nacid digestion in a microwave furnace was used.",
